  "operative_text": "Section 1 (new section in SDCL ch. 22-32): Any person who enters or remains in a motor vehicle and takes or exercises control over the property of another, and that property is a firearm or a firearm silencer, regardless of value, is guilty of a Class 5 felony. Section 2 (SDCL 22-6-11): The sentencing court shall sentence an offender convicted of a Class 5 or Class 6 felony, except those convicted under §§ 22-11A-2.1, ... section 1 of this Act, 22-42-7, subdivision 24-2-14(1), 32-23-4.6, 32-34-5, and any person ineligible for probation under § 23A-27-12, to a term of probation."
}